@startuml

title PENA-Agent — Deployment / Runtime Architecture

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

skinparam node {
  BorderColor #2F5597
  BackgroundColor #F8FBFF
}

skinparam cloud {
  BorderColor #666666
  BackgroundColor #F2F2F2
}

skinparam database {
  BorderColor #666666
  BackgroundColor #FFFCE8
}

node "Developer Laptop" as LAPTOP {

  node "VS Code + Copilot" as VSCODE

  node "Local Python Runtime" as PYTHON {

    component "PENA Runtime" as RUNTIME
    component "Observability Engine" as OBS
    component "Learning Extractor" as LEARN

  }

  database "Local Cache / Artifacts" as LOCAL

}

node "GitHub Repository" as GITHUB {
  database "Specs / UML / Context" as SPECS
}

cloud "LLM Providers" as LLM
cloud "News / RSS APIs" as NEWS

database "Observability Reports" as REPORTS

VSCODE --> GITHUB : push / pull
VSCODE --> PYTHON : run / debug

RUNTIME --> NEWS : retrieve content
RUNTIME --> LLM : summarize / analyze

RUNTIME --> OBS : emit runtime signals
OBS --> REPORTS : logs / metrics / traces

LEARN --> SPECS : learning artifacts
RUNTIME --> LOCAL : temporary outputs

GITHUB --> SPECS
PYTHON --> SPECS : load context

note bottom of PYTHON
Initial deployment remains intentionally simple:
- local runtime
- iterative experimentation
- observable execution
- human in the loop
end note

note right of SPECS
Repository specifications become active runtime grounding context.
end note

@enduml
